# Owner: check the authors below before minting a DOI (docs/adoption/README.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Husky Eye View in research or teaching, please cite it as below,
  and cite the data sources behind the layers you used (docs/METHODS.md and
  DATA_SOURCES.md).
title: "Husky Eye View: neighborhood research on a 3D globe"
abstract: >-
  Husky Eye View puts a century of U.S. neighborhood data (life expectancy,
  1930s redlining, segregation, census measures, internet access, air quality
  and green space, historical enumeration districts) on a photorealistic 3D
  globe, beside live feeds. Users can map their own files, join them to
  tracts or counties, run Stata, R, SPSS and Excel on any layer, and export
  merged data with the do-file and R script that reproduce it.
type: software
